# Tolerant fixture: a quoted entry id (Appendix C.2.4) and a list-typed field
# written as a bare scalar (Appendix C.2.1), the two relaxations that change the
# *shape* of a line rather than a tag.
#
# `emotion` and `reference` are list-typed fields; the specification has no
# single-item shorthand for them (6.1), so `emotion: objective` is a validity
# error under the strict grammar and a reported `list-shape` repair under the
# tolerant one. The quotes around the id are removed and the id is kept exactly
# as written - an identifier is never case-folded or re-spelled (5.5).
#
# Expected under `--tolerant`: FOUR repairs - one `name-quote` (the quoted id,
# line 23) and three `list-shape` (lines 27, 28, 35, one per bare list value) -
# and the ids `resolution` and `Fullscreen` present verbatim, because a parser
# MUST NOT rewrite an identifier (5.5).
# `cliff-test/tests/clarion/test_read_modes.py` asserts exactly this.
CLIFF 1.1
namespace: demo
clan: tolerant-shape
source-language: en-US
target-language: zh-CN

[video]
type: label
context: "Video settings screen."

<"resolution">
source: "Resolution"
target: "分辨率"
status: final
emotion: objective
reference: "src/ui/video.cpp:42"

<Fullscreen>
source: "Fullscreen"
target: "全屏"
status: translated
context: "Toggle on the video settings screen."
emotion: calm
